Open no window for a request stream that already ended.

lws advertises an initial stream window of 0 and gives each new stream its receive window with a WINDOW_UPDATE.
A request whose HEADERS carry END_STREAM (GET, a POST without body) sends no DATA, yet got the WINDOW_UPDATE too,
on a stream half-closed on the client's side. curl 8.23 with nghttp2 1.70 ends the connection on it (PROTOCOL_ERROR)
when the answer is not in the same read, that is for every response the server gives later (a login's delay, a
command's result). Browsers and older nghttp2 accept it.

--- a/lib/sansio/h2/http2.c
+++ b/lib/sansio/h2/http2.c
@@ -2177,8 +2177,11 @@
 			}
 		}
 
-		/* only a stream we take on gets its window */
-		if (new_stream &&
+		/*
+		 * only a stream we take on gets its window, and only one whose
+		 * peer still sends: after END_STREAM no DATA can come
+		 */
+		if (new_stream && !(h2n->flags & LWS_H2_FLAG_END_STREAM) &&
 		    lws_h2_update_peer_txcredit(h2n->swsi,
 					(unsigned int)h2n->swsi->mux.my_sid,
 					LWS_H2_STREAM_RX_CREDIT))
